fs: 2,7,5,11,6,8 \u2192 2 repeated.\n\n{0,1,3} \u2192 1,2,3,10,11,12\n{0,4,9} \u2192 4,5,9,9,8,4 \u2192 repeated.\n\n{0,1,3} \u2192 {1,2,3,10,11,12}\n{0,4,6} \u2192 {4,2,6,9,11,7} \u2192 conflicts at 2,11\n\n{0,1,4} \u2192 {1,3,4,9,12,12} \u2192 repeated 12.\n\n{0,1,3}: diffs 1,2,3,10,11,12\n{0,4,6}: diffs 4,6,2,9,7,11 \u2192 2,11 conflict\n\n{0,2,6}: diffs 2,4,6,11,9,7 \u2192 conflicts with {0,1,3} at 2,11\n\n{0,1,3},{0,4,10}: diffs of second: 4,6,10,9,7,3 \u2192 3 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,5,11}: diffs: 5,6,11,8,7,2 \u2192 2 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,4,11}: diffs: 4,7,11,9,6,2 \u2192 2 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,5,6}: diffs: 5,1,6,8,12,7 \u2192 1,12 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,4,5}: diffs: 4,1,5,9,12,8 \u2192 1,12 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,6,8}: diffs: 6,2,8,7,11,5 \u2192 2,11 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,5,7}: diffs: 5,2,7,8,11,6 \u2192 2,11 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,6,9}: diffs: 6,3,9,7,10,4 \u2192 3,10 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,6,10}: diffs: 6,4,10,7,9,3 \u2192 3 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,7,9}: diffs: 7,2,9,6,11,4 \u2192 2,11 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,4,7}: diffs: 4,3,7,9,10,6 \u2192 3,10 conflict.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,5,9}: diffs: 5,4,9,8,9,4 \u2192 repeated.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,6,7}: diffs: 6,1,7,7,12,6 \u2192 repeated.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,5,8}: diffs: 5,3,8,8,10,5 \u2192 repeated.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,4,8}: diffs: 4,4,8,9,9,5 \u2192 repeated.\n\nLet me use a known construction. For v=13, use the points of PG(2,3) minus... actually use a known BIBD(13,3,1):\n\nBase blocks mod 13: {0,1,3,9} is a (13,4,1) difference set... \n\nLet me just use two known base blocks for (13,3,1): {0,1,3} and {0,4,6} don't work. I'll use a computational approach with known result:\n\nBIBD(13,3,1) base blocks: {0,1,3}, {0,2,7}, checking: {0,2,7} diffs: 2,5,7,11,6,8. Combined with {0,1,3}: 1,2,3,5,6,7,8,10,11,12 - missing 4,9. Need a third base block covering 4,9: {0,4,9}: diffs 4,5,9,9,8,4 - repeated.\n\n{0,1,3},{0,2,7},{0,4,9} - {0,4,9} has repeated diffs. \n\nLet me try {0,1,3},{0,2,8}: diffs of second: 2,6,8,11,7,5. Combined: 1,2