,11},{0,5,9}:\n- {0,1,4}: 1,3,4,9,12,10\n- {0,8,11}: 8,3,11,5,10,2 - 3,10 conflict.\n\n{0,1,4},{0,8,11},{0,2,5}:\n- {0,1,4}: 1,3,4,9,12,10\n- {0,8,11}: 8,3,11,5,10,2 - 3,10 conflict.\n\nI keep getting conflicts. Let me try a completely different approach and look for 3 base blocks more systematically.\n\nWe need 3 base blocks B1, B2, B3 such that their difference multisets partition {1,...,12} (each appearing once).\n\nEach block {a,b,c} contributes differences: b-a, c-a, c-b, a-b, a-c, b-c (mod 13) - 6 differences.\n\n3 blocks \u00d7 6 differences = 18, but {1,...,12} has 12 elements, each appearing... wait, we need each of {1,...,12} to appear exactly 18/12... that's not integer. \n\nWait, for BIBD(13,3,1): \u03bb=1, so each pair appears in exactly 1 block. The number of blocks b=26. With 2 base blocks developed mod 13, we get 26 blocks. So we need 2 base blocks.\n\n2 blocks \u00d7 6 differences = 12 differences, covering {1,...,12} each exactly once. \u2713\n\nSo I need 2 base blocks whose difference sets partition {1,...,12}.\n\n{0,1,3}: diffs {1,2,3,10,11,12}\nNeed second block with diffs {4,5,6,7,8,9}.\n\n{a,b,c} with differences 4,5,6,7,8,9. The differences come in pairs summing to 13: (4,9),(5,8),(6,7). So the three \"positive\" differences are {4,5,6} or {4,5,7} etc., but they must form a valid triple.\n\nFor block {0,a,b} with 0<a<b<13:\ndifferences are a, b, b-a, 13-a, 13-b, 13-(b-a).\n\nWe need {a, b, b-a, 13-a, 13-b, 13-b+a} = {4,5,6,7,8,9}.\n\nThe pairs summing to 13: (4,9),(5,8),(6,7). So {a,13-a}, {b,13-b}, {b-a,13-b+a} are these pairs.\n\nCase: a=4, 13-a=9 \u2713. Then {b,13-b} and {b-4,13-b+4} must be {5,8} and {6,7}.\n- b=5: {5,8} \u2713, b-4=1 \u2192 {1,12} \u2717\n- b=6: {6,7} \u2713, b-4=2 \u2192 {2,11} \u2717\n- b=7: {7,6} \u2713, b-4=3 \u2192 {3,10} \u2717\n- b=8: {8,5} \u2713, b-4=4 \u2192 {4,9} already used \u2717\n\nCase: a=5, 13-a=8 \u2713. Then {b,13-b} and {b-5,13-b+5} must be {4,9} and {6,7}.\n- b=4: but b>a=5, no.\n- b=6: {6,7} \u2713